  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ミチタネツケバナ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%9F%E3%83%81%E3%82%BF%E3%83%8D%E3%83%84%E3%82%B1%E3%83%90%E3%83%8A",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106385279,
      "text": "ミチタネツケバナ は、アブラナ科タネツケバナ属の越年草。ヨーロッパ原産の帰化植物。乾いた路傍・農道、畔、河川の土手などに生育する雑草性の人里植物。1992年に日本新産が報告された。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cardamine hirsuta」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardamine_hirsuta",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1343589939,
      "text": "Cardamine hirsuta, commonly called hairy bittercress, popping cress, common bittercress, hoary bittercress, hairy wood-cress, small bittercress, pepperweed, shotweed, or snapweed, is an annual or biennial species of plant in the family Brassicaceae, and is edible as a salad green. It is common in moist areas around the world."
    }
  },
